-- title:
--   Group-law form of the special-fibre points dictionary
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $L\subset \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as the $L$-subfield generated by the image of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) under coefficientwise extension of scalars. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), assumed non-zero. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and an $A$-algebra. The remaining data, summarised here, consist of: two proper smooth geometrically integral curves $c_1,c_2$ over $k$ closed-immersed by $i_1,i_2$ into the base change to $k$ of the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), whose images cover it, with reduced intersection of cardinality $n>0$; sections $\varepsilon$ over $A$, $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$ over $k$, with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ the base-changed section; relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designations $D$ (over $A$, with smooth separated structural morphism and a representability witness), its base change to $k$ with an explicit witness `hreps` for the fibrewise algebraically-trivial rigidified bundles and a comparison `hPk` of Poincaré bundles, and $D_1,D_2$ for $c_1,c_2$; a morphism $\nu_2$ from the base-changed $D$ to $D_2$ whose pullbacks of Poincaré bundles agree with the rigidified pullback along $i_2$; and a datum $G$ consisting of abelian groups $J^0_s$, $J_I$, $J_E$, a subgroup $\mathrm{torus}\subseteq J^0_s$ and a surjection $\mathrm{proj}:J^0_s\to J_I\times J_E$ with kernel $\mathrm{torus}$, together with bijections $\mathrm{pts}$, $\mathrm{pts}_I$, $\mathrm{pts}_E$ of these groups onto the $k$-sections of the three designation spaces, additivity of all three in the form of isomorphisms $\mathcal{P}_{x+y}\cong\mathcal{P}_x\otimes\mathcal{P}_y$ of pulled-back Poincaré bundles, and compatibility of $\mathrm{proj}$ with post-composition by the pullback morphism along $i_1$ and by $\nu_2$. The conclusion is that $\mathrm{pts}$ is a group homomorphism for the relative group law attached to `hreps` and the group cut `algEquivZeroGroupCut`: $\mathrm{pts}(a+b)$ equals the product of $\mathrm{pts}\,a$ and $\mathrm{pts}\,b$ for all $a,b\in J^0_s$, and $\mathrm{pts}\,0$ is the unit section.
--
--   This converts the Poincaré-bundle formulation of additivity of the points dictionary on the geometric special fibre of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the stable model of $X_1(Mp)$ into the form used by consumers that compute with the scheme-theoretic relative group law. It is cited in the subsequent analysis of the special fibre, among others in the identification of the two components of $\mathrm{proj}$ with divisor class maps and in the description of the kernel of $\mathrm{proj}$ as a torus.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_pts_add_eq_relativeGroupLaw_mul_and_pts_zero_eq_one_specialFibre_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

